      "id": "acb1efa3-69db-5877-a22f-9fb1dbf7df67",
      "name": "Alert: rig unreachable"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Ask the Room: project workflow\nn8n sits **around** the rig. Everything real-time runs in Python on the Jetson (`main.py`); this workflow talks to its HTTP API.\n\n**Chat** (top): a typed question → `GET /healthz` → `POST /ask {text, source: \"n8n\"}` → the answer text. Chat questions are **text only**: the rig doesn't speak or move the laser.\n\n**Every 5 min** (bottom): `GET /state` → flags a stalled detector, no internet, lost or carried-off objects. A problem fails the execution, so it shows red under *Executions*. Swap the *Alert* nodes for Slack/Discord later.\n\nTexts (Twilio SMS) stay on the rig's own `/sms` route (signature check + whitelist); n8n isn't involved.",
        "height": 500,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -560
      ],
      "id": "b4289b25-1287-5610-ac82-747e9307c08e",
      "name": "About"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## What main.py runs (for reference, not executed here)\n```\ncamera 30 fps ─▶ detector: YOLO-World v2 (yolov8s-worldv2, config prompts)\n               ─▶ hand tracker ─▶ world model (rules) ─▶ event log (SQLite)\nclicker ─▶ Silero VAD ─▶ whisper.cpp ─▶ intent parser\n       ─▶ answer templates │ Grok (OTHER questions, online only)\n       ─▶ voice (ElevenLabs online, Piper offline) + laser pointer\ndashboard + /ask + /sms + /state  ◀─ FastAPI on :8000\n```\nDetector: the team is still comparing YOLO models; this uses the default YOLO-World v2 until that's decided (`detect.model` in `config.yaml`).",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 700,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        560,
        -560
      ],
      "id": "a2c88e9b-a9f0-5fc0-be83-31441e771652",
      "name": "Inside the rig"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Setup (self-hosted, laptop)\n1. `npx n8n` (or Docker), open http://localhost:5678, **Import from File** → `n8n/ask-the-room.json`.\n2. In **Settings**, set `rig_url`:\n   - Jetson over USB-C: `http://192.168.55.1:8000`\n   - `main.py --fake` on this laptop: `http://127.0.0.1:8000`, not `localhost` (n8n tries IPv6 `::1`; the rig listens on IPv4). Docker n8n: `http://host.docker.internal:8000`\n3. **Publish**. Open the chat trigger for the chat URL.\nNo credentials needed.",
        "height": 400,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 6
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1320,
        -560
      ],
      "id": "f73ee6ce-397f-529a-9722-a578700bcec2",
      "name": "Setup"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Grok: to do\nGrok answers OTHER questions inside the rig (`voice/llm.py`, tools `locate` / `history` / `changes_since` / `respond`).\nIts config and tool schema reference get added here next.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 3
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1320,
        200
      ],
      "id": "2e097acd-085e-567f-aa74-6ca392705963",
      "name": "Grok (next)"
    }
  ],
